# Logs
*.log

# NOTE: tests/ is deliberately TRACKED. The suite pins the regressions found
# in the Phase 12 audit (merge destroying trills, O(n^2) harmonic filter,
# count-only verification), so it has to travel with the code.
.pytest_cache/

# NOTE: HANDOFF.md is deliberately TRACKED as of Phase 13. It is the working
# brief the agreement says to update every phase, so a fresh clone that got
# HISTORY.md without it was missing half the context.

# Real-audio benchmark corpus (Phase 13).
# MAESTRO is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and this repo is MIT, so NO corpus audio or MIDI
# is ever committed. The corpus is reconstructed from benchmarks/*.json, which
# records the track list and a sha256 per file. *.wav is already ignored
# above; *.midi is NOT, and the fetcher writes .midi deliberately.
*.midi

# MAPS reference annotations (Phase 13b). The MAPS fetcher converts each piece's
# .txt annotation to .mid so `benchmark._find_pairs` can pair it with the audio.
# Those files are DERIVED FROM a CC BY-NC-SA dataset and must not be committed
# any more than the audio is. `recordings/` covers the default location, but
# `--out` can point anywhere, so the extension is ignored globally. Sample songs
# meant for the repo belong in assets/ and can be force-added.
*.mid
!assets/**/*.mid
recordings/
# Cached MAESTRO metadata (~300KB, re-fetched on demand). The manifest records
# its sha256, so the cache itself does not need to be committed.
benchmarks/.maestro-metadata.csv

# Console logs from benchmark runs. The JSON beside them is the artifact;
# these are just progress spam (ByteDance prints a line per segment).
benchmarks/real/*-stdout.txt

# Backend job working directory (Phase 4). Uploads and rendered artifacts, keyed
# by job id. *.wav / *.mp3 are already ignored above, but the artifacts this
# produces (.mid, .musicxml, .pdf, .svg) are NOT, and uploaded audio must never
# reach a commit for the same licensing reason the corpus must not.
var/

# Local backend configuration. Holds PTIFY_API_KEY when auth is enabled.
.env
